# Everything in here that is a raster is output, not source: each folder has a
# python script that regenerates it from the SVG next to it. Keeping 28 MB of
# renders in git would bury the thing that actually matters — the generators.
#
#   wallpapers/cities.py        london.png, madrid.png
#   savanna/generate.py         savanna-*.png
#   scenes/build.py             en.png/mp4, es.png/mp4
#   mascot-hats/assets.py       rhino-*.png/apng/webm
#   course-map/atlas.py         downs.png, meseta.png
#   course-map/route.py         london-*, madrid-* (the rejected first cut)
#   tab-backgrounds/skies.py    today-*, practice-*, progress-*
#   tab-backgrounds/preview.py  mock-*
#
# Run the script in a folder and its images come back byte for byte.

*.png
*.apng
*.webm
*.mp4

# Previews are scaffolding for looking at the art, not the art.
mock-*.html
*-preview.html

# The root .gitignore has a bare `generate.py`, meant for the legacy script at the
# repository root — but a pattern without a slash matches at every depth, and it
# was silently swallowing the savanna generator. Take that one back.
!generate.py
